WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
Haiti has two official
languages: Creole and French.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.830
About 95 percent of Haitians speak
Creole as their first language.

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.310
It is built on French.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.350
Yet it is not French.

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.570
Is it just French with an accent?

6
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.570
So why do most Haitians speak a
French-based language that is not French?

7
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.410
In this mission, you'll
see how colonial rule,

8
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.310
imperial power and trade carried
languages and religions around the world.

9
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.750
Then you'll find out how Brazil, the
Philippines and East Africa ended up with

10
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.830
the languages they use today.

11
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.510
Your mission: explain why most Haitians
speak a language built from French words

12
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.120
that is not French.
